    <DataNode elementId="AT1G04620-MONOMER" textLabel="7¹-hydroxychlorophyll a reductase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8GS60" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup, PMN, dreher">HCAR is a |FRAME: AT1G04620-MONOMER| based both on the elevated levels of|FRAME: CPD-7016| that can be detected in &lt;i&gt;hcar&lt;/i&gt; mutants and on enzyme assays performed using recombinant protein expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [21934147]|. HCAR localizes to the chloroplast and a truncated version of the protein lacking the putative transit sequence was used for the enzyme assays |CITS: [21934147]|. HCAR appears to associate with FAD and with an iron-sulfur cluster of undetermined stoichiometry to date. The difficult reductive elimination of a hydroxyl group reaction that is catalyzed by this enzyme appears to require the use of ferredoxin as a reducing agent |CITS: [21934147]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G04620-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G04620.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q8GS60" />
